def groups = [['key':'FRONT-OBJECTS','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:FRONT-OBJECTS','title':'Prevent front intrusion and preserve pedal clearance','model_keys':['front','pedal','barrier'],'statement':'Ahead of the AIP in front view permit only IA, fastener heads and lightweight bodywork/nosecones; rearward nuts are recommended. Front wing/mounts must move entirely aft of the AIP without contacting the front bulkhead in a frontal impact; their attachment locations aft of AIP are recommended and tabs extend at most 25 mm ahead of it. At every pedal travel/adjustment position maintain at least 25 mm clearance to the AIP rear face, all front-bulkhead structure and all noncrushable items in primary structure, including batteries/master cylinders/reservoirs.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Optional wing/bodywork installations trigger their attachment/motion conditions; pedal adjustment sweep is mandatory.'],'verification_obligation':'Inventory front-view objects, inspect tab protrusion and evaluate wing/mount crash movement if present. Sweep pedal adjustments/full travel and measure clearance to every protected structure/noncrushable object.','unresolved_decisions':['Front packaging, aerodynamic devices, adjustment ranges and collision/motion evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.6.1','F.7.2','F.8.4.3'],'source_clauses':[['F.8.6.1:p001','9f2250d52104722232c52ac4f9095c4bc4f510088596236eb6f1084e5cfe918a'],['F.8.6.1:p002','2f3eac9a32e920780a0ba35ce270f3748bd54c2596c01ef8d5c1ef2a9ea28838'],['F.8.6.2:p001','baac2a778a8eb2f3daad1aa5bfb66139a76f148d0a90364c20b1c33216f6b39c'],['F.8.6.2:p002','a24347daba5a783087d1cc656655cb0a7c5c65a40ce9fb02644ff9fef9b7befb'],['F.8.6.2:p003','dd8f8a86aa3a25901a2bd7a04c03bfcff59e48601b86b7ab16e5bcdffc05c762'],['F.8.6.2:p004','6c2940b649a7624b81d206d4885653b4262a9425ddb2b9d6f001accaa1843229'],['F.8.6.3:p001','ccfd594227b30f11363b2b72efed4db904f254feb3f6eee5d7ae6649ede4143c'],['F.8.6.3:p002','4c7d6c1bf6226e5d87e5d0351e533cc56be3766c1abcf4c068d44e252b07bc61'],['F.8.6.3:p003','9f5ed50b6edd174f69808e95cf4f6000e2e7d244acb5c1482b6cb1e995629c88'],['F.8.6.3:p004','a8fcc9cb842a882afbb7e0a2bed18a86821f5feec6a319eeab1d8135dccfbd72'],['F.8.6.3:p005','f46c73c47a7ef64000783286016d27d1ce8a9253e2d402cbf55210d3f5829b18']]],['key':'FRONT-FORCE','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:FRONT-FORCE','title':'Combine attenuator and other frontal-object forces','model_keys':['front','loadpath'],'statement':'The combined IA assembly force and force to crush/detach other objects ahead of AIP cannot exceed the F.8.8.2 peak deceleration; exclude light bodywork, light nosecones and outboard wheel assemblies. Use peak loads 95 kN for standard foam,60 kN for standard honeycomb or the measured peak for a tested IA. Demonstrate the total by testing IA and noncrushable objects together, or testing objects alone and adding the specified IA peak; alternatively calculate mounting failure from fastener shear, tearout and/or link buckling and add the corresponding IA peak.','conditions_and_alternatives':['The applicable material-dependent peak must be selected after IA choice, not combined or universally substituted.'],'verification_obligation':'Inventory included/excluded frontal objects and select an allowed test/calculation route. Check each failure mode and the correctly matched attenuator peak against the functional deceleration reference.','unresolved_decisions':['Front objects/mount failures, IA peak, proof route and combined force evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['F.8.7.1:p001','712ed09c91bc036e58bd1b725e4e0bd2e0e0d8b03aad2f43e532f37528270921'],['F.8.7.1:p002','7a8586e16e61bc70c79ce57bf43fb5a7702addf6df4925b14a98a333d96be680'],['F.8.7.2:p001','685cbf910328345be6af939c668ddae9b6f44b6c7329ffd3bb287aad4fd5a04c'],['F.8.7.2:p002','7e6cee0b3c4977d5124a263fed9e3ccf0c857ca247edd630f8d62c1a5a2a6f24'],['F.8.7.2:p003','f1f83ef06f9cfdf1d9d92878410aff332576a4adfe42b347a929c68bb9524d4f'],['F.8.7.2:p004','21c602d5a3650ab5d81f1da32bf440b0e4622a463a4d7b72fd45b50a0214b348'],['F.8.7.3:p001','66b4571f12221b632c0003d172999467462ef42f924ba211122807be8778cb48'],['F.8.7.4:p001','b769b24c1a590ce21862218b0a5004de51c5e50445c871872f07fee785621873'],['F.8.7.4:p002','d5952c1c32d90ddec299cff6967a5b53a5f849aff2f75bde8d5a155c2ae29852'],['F.8.7.4:p003','7da4df853a4cce60d213a13347d516e80b30b7781545fc38770d18dbaf6cbcfd'],['F.8.7.4:p004','9c53941bad3f6e751ed7854d04326107850eed58731e8cd6be3b77435ed2081c'],['F.8.7.5:p001','6dbd255a9620bea85ea3cbe6443891e821b09470041a0d8071b596ac44fd1331'],['F.8.7.5:p002','6f1da6c9e450e441947ea12b4cbf4e884e2a96e1a4e23f08f59a5dcec424b212'],['F.8.7.5:p003','49d9c4bc58033f2e572b352fab60a0382a80db21ce49806396eacf92ee6decd1']]],['key':'IA-PERFORMANCE','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:IA-PERFORMANCE','title':'Keep the functional impact reference separate from test criteria','model_keys':['front','loadpath'],'statement':'Include an IAD report in SES. At the rule\'s reference total vehicle mass 300 kg and impact speed 7.0 m/s, the IA functional requirement is average deceleration at most 20 g, peak at most 40 g and absorbed energy strictly above 7350 J. The source explicitly identifies these as functional requirements rather than test requirements. This does not assign a 300 kg design mass to the actual car.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Reference impact conditions are preserved, while actual vehicle mass and the substantiation method remain separate design/evidence decisions.'],'verification_obligation':'Review the IAD functional demonstration and its mass/speed/energy/deceleration derivation; assess test interpretation under the remaining F.8.8 clauses before claiming acceptance.','unresolved_decisions':['Actual vehicle design mass, IA performance and complete IAD evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['F.8.8.1:p001','de42efe93099006041e157326088590e66540cfdbf4725431f92766c26170aff'],['F.8.8.2:p001','400f9185165420b67af15c8dde333f250c2101bb8e4776470b69d07942dec2dd'],['F.8.8.2:p002','3c5f30235283352da13728e98a3cb7ace9de3a48a1360e2cda69c4bc46c939d0'],['F.8.8.2:p003','41d385e175b4ce088c2f80ffd1e194b4fb45142c6d78a712b9bb0da4d67f25eb'],['F.8.8.2:p004','618b265038757f75afae406bef9fab5e4a4d0578f6d390e58bff45a74bdb95be'],['F.8.8.2:p005','4bff21fcf3f4fc82662707d91b9f0da9665588a5fcbeb6c3f2dd630c214b7622'],['F.8.8.2:p006','3ecdf5ad0213baf1cf724a61fd830befdf1922e2ab7b44b6b77facb96c99a8a9'],['F.8.8.2:p007','4b654371afa4ac376ec0a6bedb904d94baf09d752f74a20571885f71d6593902']]],['key':'IA-EVIDENCE','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:IA-EVIDENCE','title':'Plan the applicable impact report, fixture, conduct and analysis','model_keys':['front','inspect'],'statement':'For standard IA, omit test-data submission but include all other section requirements, photos of the actual IA and evidence against its specification (supplier receipt/packing slip is allowed). Nonstandard IAD includes functional test data, energy/deceleration calculations, test schematic and photos annotated with pre/post heights; IA testing is valid only one competition year. During tests use intended IA-to-AIP attachment and a representative chassis section/fixture equivalent in strength/stiffness to baseline bulkhead, not a solid bulkhead-shaped block. Leave at least 50 mm fixture clearance behind AIP; permanent deflection anywhere is at most 25 mm beyond its pretest position. Composite IA requires dynamic testing; other constructions may use dynamic or quasi-static. Dynamic tests occur at a dedicated facility under professional/faculty supervision, not a team-built dynamic apparatus; quasi-static tests may use university facilities with the source\'s due-care advice retained. Calculate average dynamic deceleration from raw unfiltered data. If peaks exceed 40 g, the permitted filter is CFC 60(100 Hz) underSAE J211 or a 100 Hz third-order low-pass Butterworth(-3dB at 100 Hz).','conditions_and_alternatives':['Standard/custom and composite/noncomposite alternatives determine the evidence obligations; no test or approval is performed by model creation.'],'verification_obligation':'Develop the applicable IAD package; review year validity, intended assembly and representative fixture, clearances/deflection, facility/supervision and test data. Reproduce average from raw data and document any allowed filtering of peaks.','unresolved_decisions':['IA selection, dedicated facility, fixtures, current-year test data and official standard specification TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.8.8.2'],'source_clauses':[['F.8.8.3:p001','2bc5f8d43b66f12f5f27e1bd98646796596fe3609b64035848b3945516cab736'],['F.8.8.3:p002','e8742101396a5a07e3677d923a5242638d7d7ade1ae31a099a35bbc881579fae'],['F.8.8.3:p003','56aa7e358def38b56513c1dc423c08f7704696580f2acf0b261d927f8d87ecbd'],['F.8.8.3:p004','54bde9f5dfe96216be32db429a796acf0638ccb5490d02cd37b62c87d51846ba'],['F.8.8.3:p005','5f8844e90231495c2391a1ba1cc1260f3491e3f496689c3fec082b1d7f47d15f'],['F.8.8.4:p001','fbb07f69237d6718fdcf4b79ae16084f52121e6f6321323076de9f9fd833af69'],['F.8.8.4:p002','72fb9c12e54f2272cfefa2345b696dbb23bdce91b0e62995c44a58025cd15e39'],['F.8.8.4:p003','ae86a24e7662c35b094a78d41fbe671eff37d742672db185435d3f925a379d10'],['F.8.8.4:p004','94f9723f00ac8214e4bb113ab19662ea9d5e71564477ee530496b84c72f508e4'],['F.8.8.4:p005','4a5ffe3ae1e7f749e346e8c66a8244dad78f97712fa8af951edbc81ecfe34c62'],['F.8.8.5:p001','af856a84e75380151a3b00747b495c86c64da9961f30abe6a9c1f20d4ec884b2'],['F.8.8.6:p001','2a372eae8bfbfdc69dedb4071b120e9d250cc425690b892939f7ff71cb75ff89'],['F.8.8.6:p002','b67f58cf0caed59ab97a25de85c678815415b2367666c43503b4afa1ef2c4709'],['F.8.8.6:p003','7aa732189eb1bf50825089c6ffd344bcfc703d23846146c1617abce8e6922628'],['F.8.8.6:p004','45c2f7fa80b4d8ce7fb68a5aab5f9d8a6cc36c9097c22783325b2d2c3adba360'],['F.8.8.6:p005','f078efb5967d6460215390f71f7d8a40093ab7e6c07084fc5c743caaef9dfc6f'],['F.8.8.6:p006','0baf46303e553395876d3fd6418a64086881138564193b106898ed17bee2afbb'],['F.8.8.6:p007','6dfa0d048972c2ca5ddbe996f67b23401cce1c20d03c9a45ea3c82332f28e64c'],['F.8.8.7:p001','3109f564e941cb2c2cce40bd2a9f9b956710558b2d1f71c5a0ef3d0c00f0c3e7'],['F.8.8.7:p002','dabc92a6fbb6f46d29ca99b55db350b0ce9ae1cf995c448e19aefd53542fdc74'],['F.8.8.7:p003','478f5fdd43245807335b8adf43cd79180e6a1d1626c8444f1860af63f36ffd11'],['F.8.8.7:p004','8d09a48c962f55cf55a38b83e44278485b1fe3ddc06ec8a0a0339fd15b038064'],['F.8.8.7:p005','bd31949bdc609ba5fe77422a7b7ce14569b54b054bb63de6cf0e2167ce5bf88e'],['F.8.8.8:p001','ae878ac9e898ccf5890f2c32a29849dc764abb208fcca306d7c36784651f0375'],['F.8.8.8:p002','3b1cfe376541395f265a03eb9dc4b6ca0cf479f0725c777c19b12ff0531ba8ae'],['F.8.8.8:p003','c1bce2946f2e437696623cbd470582cd6664b7837f699d15a2a55b73cf41171e']]],['key':'COCKPIT-OPENING','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:COCKPIT-OPENING','title':'Keep the official cockpit opening gauge path accessible','model_keys':['accommodate','inspect'],'statement':'Pass the exact page 56 cockpit-opening gauge horizontally/parallel to ground, inserted vertically from above intervening structure/bodywork between hoops, allowing fore/aft translation, until both at least 25 mm below the side-impact top\'s lowest point and at most 320 mm above the cockpit\'s lowest point. Gauge drawing dimensions are 600 mm overall fore/aft span, front transverse 400 mm, rear transverse 350 mm,100 mm rear bevel offset, and 75/100 mm top-profile offsets; use the actual official outline rather than treating those dimensions as a rectangular substitute. Wheel/column/seat/padding removal is permitted, but retain the firewall; retain shifter/shift/clutch unless integral with the removed wheel. Routing cannot obstruct the gauge. In practice the column remains and may be maneuvered around, never around fixed supports; an optional front-center column slot is allowed.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Gauge outline and orientation are checked visually against the source drawing; T.1.2 internal cross-section remains outside this bounded interpretation.'],'verification_obligation':'Construct the exact official gauge and document permitted/forbidden removals, unchanged firewall, routing and fixed supports. Demonstrate insertion to both limits without replacing the prescribed geometry.','unresolved_decisions':['Cockpit opening/bodywork geometry, removable equipment and physical gauge demonstration TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.6.4','F.7.5.1','T.1.2'],'source_clauses':[['T.1.1.1:p001','031ca913e45300fc0243226e418cd1bc0b9538ad07239c3c977504cad344eee5'],['T.1.1.2:p001','933797858dbd9b7336b4b4de2f281fc3ea486b3c4dce830c81eaa77217fafe86'],['T.1.1.2:p002','b58c67a5a232d13e401ae607f9ece350db387c36f795dba732b73d2364c3b8f3'],['T.1.1.2:p003','d978f7e9466c2950a4d1111d312e77c93c9fe3dae5bc694d3b6e0f7adfcea4c9'],['T.1.1.3:p001','adced159034026eb3db6a4bffbe510a289df82980d1f02414caf02a5b5f8a855'],['T.1.1.4:p001','d74851b18a840601614631b64c662e10b5dabebb19b0354987207408adc0007e'],['T.1.1.4:p002','bc9bb4e8d4a56e2c43116fb39d1ffb13e1041febbddc1990c4e64d68a25a840f'],['T.1.1.4:p003','791ea08d1d7aaf5c5608e066b0f7301b5f71f5d55b05b24d5b3ceabccb2447d0'],['T.1.1.4:p004','010ae0b23ee23e604d03120fdde00447628a2e6ca646b4620868e69c2d83d224'],['T.1.1.4:p005','6b5a3dfe7f4e2b553d66816b27705a280c0bef6c68a12753446711752e1f95ff'],['T.1.1.4:p006','d92e61304a027114d4939be492c336ea07b819e2aead362f5832a06194d00b1d'],['T.1.1.4:p007','36b69471b653ea0d4441a6371d945a8b96a77e3c4da8c9f1a45c741e2160a750']]],['key':'COCKPIT-PROTECTION','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:COCKPIT-PROTECTION','title':'Contain the occupant and shield moving/sharp hazards','model_keys':['accommodate','barrier','loadpath'],'statement':'Contain hips entirely within major chassis structure. With feet on pedals, feet/legs ahead of the front hoop stay inside/below structural tubing or equivalent in front/side views. Shield every moving suspension/steering part and sharp edge in the cockpit from the front hoop to a plane 100 mm behind pedals using solid material, including springs, dampers, rockers, antiroll bars, rack and column CV joints; make covers removable for mounting-point inspection. Protect the seat by keeping its lowest point at/above the upper surface of the lowest structural tube/equivalent in side view, or by a longitudinal class B side-impact tube below it.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Seat protection alternatives remain unresolved; shields are functional hazards barriers, not permanent inspection obstructions.'],'verification_obligation':'Check hips/feet/legs for all drivers and pedal settings, inspect the full hazard zone and removable shields, and measure the selected seat-protection alternative.','unresolved_decisions':['Cockpit fit, hazard shields, seat and protection layout TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['T.1.3.1:p001','d8f8063599186f2fc17d8bec58d2d9967f3ee1802ff3cf64d935e2dec4e07318'],['T.1.3.2:p001','f883fdf1781f9f0eff4acb088725887444b40ea3f0b77e2aeb5f2ab038e97aee'],['T.1.3.3:p001','7b1d58e116897f81f250a565c3beda311a46b581239d90f2af2020263d5fe4a5'],['T.1.3.3:p002','a162eab22e92527248b275bf5aa4fcf2a9fe0690c6b03acf3a360f3c0a88176f'],['T.1.3.4:p001','48a0ae7d94ffb135cc9c1fdb02da4dc4d1d52d603f02e58f160ff91cea6fa6c5'],['T.1.5.1:p001','88e8c39a2501fa48d352e0b1c3c2e4bb7e9f2a6e9cf07ebb14b122e6b1f7ab9c'],['T.1.5.1:p002','799d0685a01e876706b6641ebb5df3d3d88ae8affccbe6334c9146a98e47c52b'],['T.1.5.1:p003','6e72cb63c639d9c284d852532e6e4e5ba79137f78aaa86660dec022c2a0b3f89']]],['key':'FLOOR','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:FLOOR','title':'Exclude track debris with a continuous floor closeout','model_keys':['barrier'],'statement':'Provide a solid nonbrittle floor closeout from the feet to the firewall to keep track debris out; gaps between multiple panels are at most 3 mm.','conditions_and_alternatives':['All vehicles; panel count and material remain unresolved.'],'verification_obligation':'Inspect material, foot-to-firewall coverage and every panel gap; demonstrate debris exclusion and attachment integrity under the selected environment.','unresolved_decisions':['Floor material, joints and attachment design TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['T.1.7.1:p001','e7e1b23067390ac47ed41e69e96ede1c813ef5fb2c3d11700f81e2b1965ac9d4'],['T.1.7.2:p001','c6bf5aea236607dbf366453535d166845b78d30889e9afe841248dc364b800f2'],['T.1.7.3:p001','896ec968a2b5e7c10683564e0aa51c5c66ce66b81460c5f33a0a9cc81677aa95'],['T.1.7.4:p001','1462e1c1f1f353c11557e64735a7c3c96ace53307fbf92f6d8a71bb0e129c06b']]],['key':'FIREWALL','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:FIREWALL','title':'Isolate occupants and harness from fluids, batteries and TS','model_keys':['barrier','accommodate'],'statement':'Separate the driver compartment and every harness portion from fuel-system components if present, engine oil if present, liquid cooling and lithium batteries; for EV additionally separate all TS components except the specified outboard wheel motors and their cables at wheels/front arms. Extend the firewall so no body point less than 100 mm above the tallest driver\'s helmet bottom has direct sight to those hazards. Use a tightly mounted rigid nonflammable impermeable surface. For EV/lithium batteries, the battery/TS-side firewall layer is aluminum (not aluminum tape) and grounded per EV.7.7; the tractive battery container cannot serve as firewall. Seal the whole surface, edges, joints, passthroughs and floor against fluids; overlap/seal multi-panel joints, keep inter-firewall sealing unstressed, use passthrough grommets and environmentally rated sealants/adhesives.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Human-driven EV baseline; conditional oil/fuel/cooling/lithium hazards must be inventoried, not silently declared absent.','Only the specific outboard-motor/cable exception is retained; it does not exempt the rest of TS.'],'verification_obligation':'Inventory all hazards/harness paths and inspect sightlines for tallest driver, layers, ground path, container separation, mounts and complete seals/grommets. Substantiate material flammability/permeability and environmental ratings.','unresolved_decisions':['Firewall geometry, aluminum layer/grounding, fluids/battery/cooling inventory and seals TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['EV.4.1.3','EV.7.7'],'source_clauses':[['T.1.8.1:p001','1fd8f024937d233376d4f2e6c1ceeb4075f9dd2fc70c923ee8f0f9bdda359e48'],['T.1.8.1:p002','17ea30bed5048733ef31fe6b98ecb0187bc5bf31551a09023e9e26a4453aef26'],['T.1.8.1:p003','abad6f3839334df4697fd6f2031e1bc829c0fdc69a9ecd886fd7456eec3c4fff'],['T.1.8.2:p001','8d8ccdcf2da8eeb8982a886ef320992540ace5bac413391322f38065dce232f7'],['T.1.8.3:p001','4fbe8906c5823e5f3c3273a7a2dd3071b41081440ea81346ba1e6c3e708e29ce'],['T.1.8.3:p002','a03a29256141f8658ed6f41639d5a0c7d5c7c4c2d7efd65681d50391acdf5295'],['T.1.8.3:p003','976c92cf79df8e60247366f8ea1af215718df2348a61fdf14eb4e8e8cd437441'],['T.1.8.4:p001','0d78cd31e0807d6894230ac40b5ad19d2eb0beee7f44304dd2a16c4a37cad795'],['T.1.8.4:p002','b4a5ae58943ea1490771482be357bf464c090af529593f545202917b6a0dc934'],['T.1.8.4:p003','fc360642de41385e6da319cb79d2904fc5a196e677dd650d23d8e11c766e4870'],['T.1.8.4:p004','edc27fa4f2fa887c8cb2be28f1dd3a78fd9309d5d1e74bdac9bcaf6ee3f3293b'],['T.1.8.5:p001','845aee4e1637ed1549a14f2e952086550a3d7438cbe70b64f28361b4a3df0591'],['T.1.8.6:p001','4253ab5a548b493f5265a9ec1b37670f72c2a38403c42d72a56e4d6dcbb832a4'],['T.1.8.6:p002','8aaefd00b3de75aff2d3ac34e3b7e96d3ab3d96cb7392b31f185a3ae1d43a67d'],['T.1.8.6:p003','4966d517b32947fd921e2572f89c320d9e5115fde4f0b6774a38c1906d2b3412'],['T.1.8.6:p004','1e57cd77b905386b61688b96e388eb3bf0100e240dea81b85d3743d571a2d806'],['T.1.8.6:p005','bee557b159f4ac621f76ada0754f3518865b813b26e7308567b6cb5ef185bac6'],['T.1.8.6:p006','7822538c04e8df94f2f17cb7df7ccce0fe86e037036e3730ef9e7b24dbf58e51']]],['key':'HARNESS','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:HARNESS','title':'Retain certified harness and posture-dependent alternatives','model_keys':['restrain','accommodate'],'statement':'Select a 5-,6- or 7-point harness certified to SFI 16.1, SFI 16.5 orFIA 8853/2016. Keep original labels/specification/expiration, use within the labeled expiration year (expiry on/before 31December of the competition calendar year is permitted), keep new/like-new condition without wear/cuts/chafing, follow manufacturer installation/threading and never modify supplied hardware. Five points are two lap/two shoulder/one antisubmarine belt; six use two lap/two shoulder/two leg or antisubmarine belts; seven add a negative-g/Z belt. Template seat-back angle at most 30 degrees is upright, strictly above 30 degrees is reclined; the chest-to-groin line follows shoulder belts to release buckle in side view. Reclined requires 6/7 points and either quick-adjust antisubmarine belts or two installed sets. All lap belts have tilt-lock quick adjusters; pull-up over pull-down is recommended. Use separate over-shoulder straps, neverY straps; H configuration is allowed.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Posture, exact harness and certificate/specification remain unselected. Belt mount strength/angles are not claimed by this specification-only group.'],'verification_obligation':'Select posture and harness, audit original manufacturer certification/expiration/condition/instructions/unmodified hardware, count belt paths and inspect required adjusters/strap geometry. Review all referenced mounting clauses separately.','unresolved_decisions':['Driving posture, harness model, expiration, manufacturer documentation and mounting design TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['T.2.4','T.2.5','T.2.6','T.2.7'],'source_clauses':[['T.2.1:p001','b67c52f57b7cb61d951e43355214885cd3508c1977e34d7a015ca70495210191'],['T.2.1:p002','41b0456a81900d6129443c6eaa18c5840342b29e3051352b9c91341f283eb653'],['T.2.1:p003','1185a421e38939c3b688ad32d23d10798b71fef7acbb342840d67fec5b29c838'],['T.2.1:p004','7fcbe32fff97ff63e10c25aef735eab53801796b4327f69c4e051cd24ed08697'],['T.2.1:p005','de0707adb74ffd3c9597b08632c4e97771a5cb2da76a9a1473e32d8080abb7a3'],['T.2.1:p006','1d0a4d27b24a7eb5d1e91fe54518db6c72275e5e1d3af5b774881886b7607630'],['T.2.2.1:p001','34443ed8ea291dc97d46903e4f13c491ad358ed419f01bf8a023b561892bc81a'],['T.2.2.1:p002','52bb7b72bab9aa3b74151a31f25b01960b5b4f4e5f2ca4a42993b030a22ee853'],['T.2.2.1:p003','ba81413503d0a35aca21d00260f69a1129271f2bbe2204689a085895031f650b'],['T.2.2.1:p004','8c2e55972e373bc8ea827bcc399394d8dbe44119d2d283dff80369b21d9a47fe'],['T.2.2.2:p001','11326ee2cffb6acefdffae5532be836c05fffbd96c8356deb4b5117fce6fd77a'],['T.2.2.3:p001','deaeb838daa2415db9e50670610aae3702389ae081d22862823ae54692c532d5'],['T.2.2.4:p001','f0593f387f4d9e02d7693f6845365b31b07869d8835ef04559a8da088fc26461'],['T.2.2.5:p001','bc4e2a61a6bdd47bbcab4dbf30270369f3ee563e2c693f0bbf4df0d48f27c097'],['T.2.2.6:p001','9f545192fa6ed978f360dc9d093bf8bf5488f85fc174f392873a25edbfbfd476'],['T.2.3.1:p001','2f319cb7afe8934bf77c3c5eaa272746ede80b81d58100563708567183a3d49d'],['T.2.3.1:p002','5baeb5d92ee753b996d6d66007f35697a48b206e612422972627fef0bc53fd03'],['T.2.3.1:p003','bb895195cf0719fe35fb26d8edb862d7174d914708a5025992a9b6203d150480'],['T.2.3.1:p004','1cfa25c8c8e870d05694895fd1ba6d9b6d1f3a164b3accc94afbe6a34ca3d0c5'],['T.2.3.1:p005','f8d019f16b331574564e040e4d04a56e68d2e4b7107da4b83f7cf707a8c6e885'],['T.2.3.2:p001','47a52aea2fd95b12aaababca19efbd735247c199753e65c351400deec5d997f9'],['T.2.3.2:p002','cb415da68cbbedd3121ee19b22ec1810cf5fcf3f4f49bafe4c4451860135bbe2'],['T.2.3.3:p001','d8dbd708282bb58c6f200fef045eda12c716df0f0fb671d00bd0acac55a443d8']]],['key':'HEAD','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:HEAD','title':'Provide and substantiate adjustable head restraint','model_keys':['head','restrain','rollover'],'statement':'Limit rearward head movement with a vertical/near-vertical head restraint entirely inside the rollover envelope or permitted head-restraint protection. Do not attach other items to its material/structure or place items 25 mm or less away. Attach near top and bottom with strength at any load point strictly above 900 N rearward and 300 N lateral/vertical. For every driver, helmet rear gap is at most 25 mm and contact at least 50 mm from every edge. Approximate 100 mm longitudinal adjustment or multiple thicknesses is a source accommodation suggestion. Padding satisfiesSFI 45.2 or specified blue CONFOR CF45/CF45M underFIA List 17, is at least 38 mm thick and 15 cm wide, and has either area at least 235 cm^2 plus total height adjustment at least 17.5 cm or height at least 28 cm. Cover it with thin flexible material and an approximately 20 mm inspection hole on a nonfront surface.','conditions_and_alternatives':['All drivers; material/area-adjustment versus fixed-height alternative and protection-envelope choice remain unresolved.'],'verification_obligation':'Inspect approved padding/cover/hole, containment and item exclusion; measure fit for all drivers and the selected geometry alternative. Substantiate mounts under loads applied anywhere with the strict strength inequalities.','unresolved_decisions':['Head-restraint material, geometry/adjustment, mounts, proof loads and envelope alternative TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.1.13','F.5.10'],'source_clauses':[['T.2.8.1:p001','a31638166e369362772b363889a6e1fdb885d408f4c291a2b653cfdc69b1ddf5'],['T.2.8.2:p001','00079c6f238759859609c6386e98fdec8ce41207b1375e4830f1154a160a6b3e'],['T.2.8.3:p001','7d5d08ea8cfa530e28363f8af7032d2a2fe7d805e47fa0ad4d545645ee8189fe'],['T.2.8.3:p002','a1297f68474fa1a58c99d5f6a4b9a46ffeedd8077de2f2afcd68f1649dc5e279'],['T.2.8.3:p003','9ac2bbc31522198ff289a4b2384edffe66400b5e2d7e5b93d41631e7f848de94'],['T.2.8.4:p001','60184ae102fcc92d9a5dd438fda3f7bf96d86a734f38ee62d56a7389f628cda4'],['T.2.8.4:p002','22c20ffc5c62714306141382afdb4c0ba2abb987d8498cbb6020794ad21b7008'],['T.2.8.4:p003','43fba88343ff41d5f102413272749b88deff19d7b6ecea395cc4763df974cecd'],['T.2.8.5:p001','760d789c5016bc2dba793e152d7412b008ebdcc385399ae111c4fd4af9171890'],['T.2.8.5:p002','701753bf80ce7bd4005bf78e1be18ad5e5cf4a809d9a2b2869349