[],'source_clauses':[['T.2.9:p001','20fbdaa01579de4e84b227501d4cc11928e44b37f5045ce6ac6c81ff0e9f2f78']]],['key':'BRAKE-CORE','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:BRAKE-CORE','title':'Maintain hydraulic stopping under a circuit failure','model_keys':['brake-demand','hydraulic-a','hydraulic-b','friction','protect-brakes'],'statement':'Provide brakes on all four wheels operated by a single control and able to lock all four. Use two independent hydraulic circuits; leakage/failure at any point leaves effective braking on at least two wheels. Each circuit has a separate fluid reserve via separate reservoirs or an OEM-style reservoir. A single brake on a limited-slip differential is permitted, not selected. Prohibit brake-by-wire and unarmored plastic lines. Use scatter shielding against drivetrain failure and minor collisions. Sprung brake components in side view do not project below the chassis lower surface. Treat every brake-system fastener as critical under T.8.2.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Circuit wheel assignment and differential versus wheel-brake hardware remain unresolved; a common electronics/regen path cannot replace hydraulic braking.','Separate reserves in an OEM-style housing do not waive hydraulic circuit independence.'],'verification_obligation':'Inspect single mechanical control, hydraulic separation/reserves/materials, critical fasteners, shielding and sprung packaging. Demonstrate four-wheel lock and inject every credible leak/failure to prove effective braking on at least two wheels.','unresolved_decisions':['Circuit split, reservoirs, cylinders/calipers/differential, lines, shields, fasteners and performance evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['T.5.2','T.8.2'],'source_clauses':[['T.3.1.1:p001','2b04ff49da7d9159abb34c83773ed1c1d5e5ac13b52f63a9415a2602f204b761'],['T.3.1.2:p001','bb78980ae4974cd44ec3ad8941ef05116537413d173ef96781389b25cfccf6be'],['T.3.1.2:p002','636f179ced0d971b5e8c54895e831c7548cc564eab20e350a1d2dfaa6c614249'],['T.3.1.2:p003','244d2da9ec40ec02fcf4c5c389fcee7c90812ec7aa6aeef9a4a50f21e2ec2485'],['T.3.1.2:p004','a832690b249c4328cdfb626036928096ea069b4ad22be35ac71abd814ca1189c'],['T.3.1.3:p001','b6ecc07446f84d712027a34b7ec5c566ce6893db7c605f94b63090d5be076047'],['T.3.1.3:p002','cdd0fc8f2305d7d532971c7a2fd9bd5fcb4f386e01a7a579b3ac4a66911bff37'],['T.3.1.4:p001','08004376d76f88ebcb7f2b7518b7c31ffa1fd996c7092556556b21d6e7f3685c'],['T.3.1.5:p001','4ec5c4081de0859646483c0c9242187217dc367285c741f3b5e51b57d9148a3d'],['T.3.1.6:p001','68f6fc613a6256f5ebcb7df94056a8e33dcaa34fe0f3f6ad4e56eb0600fdf300'],['T.3.1.7:p001','4b44d36069bcb4847fda0335e6494dc216269d33ad37df3185ad55f6e0f142bb'],['T.3.1.8:p001','3c9d44c6b9f0bf7ca231ec2135d06b0deea5b13b9fc16bb97948e5e1b5ee4f63'],['T.3.1.9:p001','fea9214addb5d3f5804f53f9bf11408fd1c6759222da188a6f04cefe79a46663'],['T.3.1.10:p001','292aec2c7e8d5997846a16518bd78e0408e8ecf1336b2341892ea1d374e7d2cb']]],['key':'PEDAL','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:PEDAL','title':'Protect mechanical pedal strength and operation','model_keys':['pedal','brake-demand','hydraulic-a','hydraulic-b'],'statement':'Pedal material/manufacture is fabricated steel/aluminum or machined steel/aluminum/titanium. Pedal and associated parts withstand at least 2000 N without failure of brakes, box, chassis mount or adjustment. The source explicitly says this is not a design criterion and allows seated-official maximum-force pedal testing; a 2000 N calculation alone is not accepted as completed design verification. Failure of non-loadbearing brake/box parts must never obstruct pedal or brake operation.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Material and fabrication route are coupled alternatives; fabricated titanium is not an allowed listed option.'],'verification_obligation':'Review selected material/process, load path and hazards from non-loadbearing failures. Substantiate the minimum strength and inspection pedal-test conditions with documented test/analysis evidence, not an invented universal design margin.','unresolved_decisions':['Pedal fabrication/material, box/mount/adjustment, human force envelope and proof evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['T.3.2.1:p001','c6f2cc06c357bd43c9c595a2200fc6093e2a9585b32267584a648da71d657ccb'],['T.3.2.1:p002','8263b64f64e7f791f9b52c194e63d1db6d14977277bc63b7628cb50b04ce2862'],['T.3.2.1:p003','7a59a258f2f19c1326ee7f62d818327e4fc861c76c6e143652b812ad845428b1'],['T.3.2.2:p001','205f96c375dc7059e6e28b18da7fe97190cd1a6923e5560c4386866c285a7262'],['T.3.2.2:p002','38b33c557c5c7e5cab518fa29d118619a9c6225b1333eee97f15712cc409eeef'],['T.3.2.3:p001','930cacc418e22d4f07077be3b29266826a86ae011cda26c34cb583266edd2e1b']]],['key':'BRAKE-REGEN','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:BRAKE-REGEN','title':'Keep regenerative braking optional and hydraulic actuation direct','model_keys':['brake-demand','friction'],'statement':'For this EV the first 90 percent of pedal travel may regenerate without hydraulic actuation; it is an option. The remaining travel directly operates hydraulics, and regeneration may remain active. No 90 percent deadband or regeneration strategy is selected until the complete brake/powertrain design is reviewed.','conditions_and_alternatives':['If regeneration is used, coordinate the low-speed inhibition and brake/accelerator plausibility in the separately owned driver-demand slice.'],'verification_obligation':'Decide whether and how regen is used; sweep pedal travel and prove direct hydraulic actuation in the remaining range even with disabled/failed regeneration. Review the referenced EV regenerative braking and conflict safeguards.','unresolved_decisions':['Regen adoption, pedal transition, hydraulic timing and cross-slice interface contract TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['EV.4.6','EV.3.3.3','EV.4.7'],'source_clauses':[['T.3.2.4:p001','8df4d4a102b8d54185d2c6ff9b67f9e29f5ba4f57be821756d15cbc980e01927'],['T.3.2.4:p002','1b9c131492922f48c19675d837b7ea4d689970d34aab2bf92ef781bfd4a9b098'],['T.3.2.4:p003','111946fcd230d7a76e9c01f19f718fc502ad9ddaef9afdbd471640e57fd40b75']]],['key':'BOTS','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:BOTS','title':'Open and retain the direct overtravel shutdown contact','model_keys':['overtravel','pedal'],'statement':'Travel beyond the normal brake-pedal range operates BOTS. Use a mechanical SPST two-position push-pull, push-rotate or flip switch that holds OFF; OFF opens the EV shutdown circuit. The driver cannot reset it. Implement the circuit with analog components, excluding programmable logic/ECU/similar digital controllers. The model reuses the shutdown slice\'s physical BOTS contact rather than adding a parallel or duplicate contact.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Human-driven EV: EV.8.2.2 applies; the published IC reference is retained as nonapplicable to this electric baseline.'],'verification_obligation':'Force brake overtravel, inspect mechanical SPST/contact holding and analog/direct wiring, prove the installed series shutdown opens and verify no seated/restrained driver can reset the contact.','unresolved_decisions':['Overtravel threshold, normal travel/adjustment limits, switch rating/location and reset-access geometry TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['EV.8.2.2'],'source_clauses':[['T.3.3.1:p001','05fdaf186837dfc9b409767da199fea1c3a63297f5ffa7336a750e8e7dab5d80'],['T.3.3.2:p001','c04cd6cd3b857f4cc38d8860c88d53b8ff44e4b12d11884905c63b5a52ffba49'],['T.3.3.2:p002','89390624f593c5758f268d63884859fd03fbafb696fcfe7317f51196b617c1f2'],['T.3.3.2:p003','f59aa0afdee48dd9e87c9e771197207e0b01db3fa151a28bde6f822d0720abdd'],['T.3.3.3:p001','b7f490feac1f1a19c29341796386c6480a7df6e9441c036206dcc5fcaf53b057'],['T.3.3.4:p001','f632461dc0ddf373bacd21873bb856e0a54fbd47edf2d0397f198231a84bbe99'],['T.3.3.5:p001','01538ae822040f87711f8fd933078991846246c7748454e3fa70ac17f5f40406']]],['key':'BRAKE-LIGHT','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:BRAKE-LIGHT','title':'Signal braking with the required rear visibility and geometry','model_keys':['brake-light','brake-demand'],'statement':'Provide a rear brake lamp plainly visible in very bright sunlight. It is red on black, rectangular/triangular/near-round with lit area at least 15 cm^2, vertically between wheel centerline and driver\'s shoulder and approximately on lateral centerline. Undiffused LEDs are at most 20 mm apart; a single LED line is at least 150 mm long. These alternatives do not override minimum lit area/visibility.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Lamp shape, LED/diffuser technology, brightness and trigger circuit remain unresolved.'],'verification_obligation':'Inspect color/background, shape/lit area and installation heights/centerline. Apply the conditional LED spacing/line-length checks and demonstrate visibility from rear in very bright sunlight with the chosen brake activation logic.','unresolved_decisions':['Exact lamp, wiring/activation, diffuser/LED layout and sunlight visibility evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['T.3.4.1:p001','512f20f7d7d1ddec90eebf00321ca54470ad19a84f5a58953bc8414ab504223f'],['T.3.4.2:p001','fddd0bdf67dadf4ca6e2dac16fddd91b35c8b5df66b56518dd554c88fc21c59e'],['T.3.4.2:p002','7f5cdf4eac451d5cc118575f2d8c644ac8b57a66afd7007ae6b8f22e36606ef4'],['T.3.4.2:p003','526c82704363688f658d3ebd8ffb5ec279302df0c4f697cb6e86af0a7a9b3029'],['T.3.4.2:p004','ec7c45cdfff3a970674c4ebaa3bec84b437acaca3bc947ab782bb6de5d7e59ee'],['T.3.4.3:p001','25111a5e445c47307c44ff9e9a5cff5ea0c2d51b91ab6b059149963808b144c9'],['T.3.4.4:p001','2b635cfc5c585768908ed222b62a4152cc7a14e5ddf8f73b88fdd37f2ff7973d']]]]
groups.each { group -> group.source_clauses = group.source_clauses.collect { source -> [clause_id:'FSAE-2027-V1:' + source[0], source_text_sha256:source[1]] } }
def sourceModule = req.find('FSAE-2027-V1:source-module')
def derivedModule = req.find('FSAE2027:VP:derived-module')
def folder = req.find('FSAE2027:VP:derived-folder')
assert sourceModule != null && derivedModule != null && folder != null && folder.eContainer() == derivedModule
assert req.requirements(derivedModule).size() == 16:
    'Run batches once, in order. Existing requirements need review rather than overwrite.'
def sources = req.requirements(sourceModule).collectEntries { [(it.ReqIFIdentifier):it] }
assert sources.size() == 3197
groups.each { group ->
    assert req.find(group.identifier) == null
    assert api.findById(stableId('constraint:VERIFY-' + group.key)) == null
    group.source_clauses.each { source ->
        def requirement = sources[source.clause_id]
        assert requirement != null: 'Missing exact pinned source ' + source.clause_id
        def attributes = req.attributes(requirement)
        assert attributes.source_sha256 == 'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e' && attributes.source_text_sha256 == source.source_text_sha256
        assert attributes.verification_status == 'not_verified': 'Existing evidence needs review'
        assert attributes.vehicle_protection_slice_id == null: 'Existing scoped source allocation needs review'
    }
}
def owners = [loadpath:'loadpath',rollover:'rollover',side:'side',front:'front',accommodate:'accommodate',barrier:'barrier',
    restrain:'restrain',head:'head',pedal:'pedal','brake-demand':'pedal','hydraulic-a':'hydraulic-a','hydraulic-b':'hydraulic-b',
    friction:'friction','protect-brakes':'friction',overtravel:'overtravel','brake-light':'brake-light',inspect:'accommodate']
def existingBots = api.findById(java.util.UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes('FSAE2027:SD:node:BOTS'.getBytes('UTF-8')).toString())
assert existingBots != null && existingBots.nature == PhysicalComponentNature.NODE
def jsonStrings = { values ->
    '[' + values.collect { '"' + it.toString().replace('\\','\\\\').replace('"','\\"').replace('\n','\\n').replace('\r','\\r') + '"' }.join(',') + ']'
}
def state = [slice_id:sliceId,batch:2,candidate_obligations:[:],verification_status:'not_verified',design_status:'unresolved']
api.batch('Trace bounded vehicle protection candidate obligations batch 2') {
    groups.each { group ->
        def derived = req.create(folder, group.identifier, prefix + group.title, group.statement)
        [source_document_id:'FSAE-2027-V1',source_sha256:'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e',slice_id:sliceId,
            interpretation_status:'bounded_source_interpretation_requires_design_review',coverage_status:'allocated_candidate_design',
            verification_status:'not_verified',design_status:'unresolved',conditions_and_alternatives:jsonStrings(group.conditions_and_alternatives),
            unresolved_decisions:jsonStrings(group.unresolved_decisions),dependent_source_rules:jsonStrings(group.dependent_source_rules),
            source_clause_ids:jsonStrings(group.source_clauses.collect { it.clause_id })].each { key, value -> req.setAttribute(derived, key, value) }
        def represented = group.model_keys.collectMany { key ->
            def owner = owners[key]
            ['OA','SA','LA','PA'].collect { element('function:' + it + ':' + key) } +
                [element('logical:' + owner),element('behavior:' + owner),owner == 'overtravel' ? existingBots : element('node:' + owner),element('ci:' + owner)]
        }.unique()
        represented.each { req.satisfy(it, derived) }
        def verification = api.create('Constraint', prefix + group.title + ' verification NOT_VERIFIED', api.layer('SA'))
        assert api.set(verification, 'id', stableId('constraint:VERIFY-' + group.key))
        def expression = org.polarsys.capella.core.data.information.datavalue.DatavalueFactory.eINSTANCE.createOpaqueExpression()
        expression.languages.add('Text')
        expression.bodies.add(group.verification_obligation + '\nConditions/alternatives: ' + group.conditions_and_alternatives.join(' ') +
            '\nOpen choices: ' + group.unresolved_decisions.join(' ') + '\nDependencies outside this bounded interpretation: ' + group.dependent_source_rules.join(', ') +
            '\nNOT_VERIFIED: a verification obligation, not an executed test or compliance statement.')
        verification.ownedSpecification = expression
        verification.constrainedElements.addAll(represented)
        verification.summary = 'NOT_VERIFIED. Candidate source-grounded verification; construction and evidence remain unresolved.'
        req.verify(derived, verification)
        group.source_clauses.each { source ->
            def requirement = sources[source.clause_id]
            req.derive(derived, requirement)
            represented.each { req.satisfy(it, requirement) }
            req.verify(requirement, verification)
            req.setAttribute(requirement, 'vehicle_protection_slice_id', sliceId)
            req.setAttribute(requirement, 'vehicle_protection_interpretation_status', 'bounded_source_interpretation_requires_design_review')
            req.setAttribute(requirement, 'vehicle_protection_coverage_status', 'allocated_candidate_design')
            req.setAttribute(requirement, 'vehicle_protection_verification_status', 'not_verified')
            req.setAttribute(requirement, 'vehicle_protection_model_element_ids', jsonStrings(represented.collect { api.id(it) }))
            req.setAttribute(requirement, 'vehicle_protection_verification_element_ids', jsonStrings([api.id(verification)]))
        }
        state.candidate_obligations[group.key] = [identifier:derived.ReqIFIdentifier,source_paragraphs:group.source_clauses.size(),verification:api.id(verification)]
    }
}
assert req.requirements(derivedModule).size() == 32
log.info('Vehicle-protection trace batch 2 applied. All construction decisions and physical verification remain unresolved.')
return state
